{# Section eyebrow: mono label preceded by a small square marker, optionally
   opened by the section number.
   Params: text, number (optional, e.g. '01'), tone ('light' default, 'dark'
   for a dark ground).

   The tone is not decoration. The purple measures 2.80:1 on the neutral-950
   band where the dark tone is used, and misses AA there, so that tone carries
   the brighter step.

   The separator takes neutral-500 on both tones. It had the ramp the wrong
   way round — neutral-400 measured 2.38:1 on the neutral-100 sections and
   neutral-600 measured 2.54:1 on the band. neutral-500 carries both
   (4.34:1 and 4.18:1) and stays a step quieter than the label.

   The number is the curriculum-vitae convention this site adds to the family
   vocabulary: it structures a long single page without a table of
   contents. #}
{% set tone = tone|default('light') %}
<p class="flex items-center gap-3 font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] {{ tone == 'dark' ? 'text-neutral-400' : 'text-neutral-600' }}">
    <span aria-hidden="true" class="inline-block h-2 w-2 shrink-0 rounded-[2px] {{ tone == 'dark' ? 'bg-accent-on-dark' : 'bg-accent' }}"></span>
    {%- if number is defined and number %}<span class="font-semibold {{ tone == 'dark' ? 'text-accent-on-dark' : 'text-accent-on-light' }}">{{ number }}</span><span class="text-neutral-500" aria-hidden="true">—</span>{% endif -%}
    {{ text }}
</p>
